stream
<?xpacket begin="ï»¿" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?>
<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">I Thought I Was Just Haunted (Then I Saw You On My TV Screen)</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;Meanwhile, Adora Eternia has got her life on lockdown. She's in a pop band (whose work is not respected by others in the industry.) She has a steady record deal (and has to endure a steady stream of besuited menaces telling her how to do her job.) She went to Juilliard (and lost her ex-best &lt;em&gt;everything&lt;/em&gt; along the way.) &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Yup. Totally got this under control.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;At least until said ex-best "it's complicated" reenters her life via Adora's television screen. Now Adora's finally got the chance at getting ten years worth of overdue answers, if she doesn't end up strangling Catra first.&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>MalachiWalker</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
      </dc:creator>
      <dc:subject>
        <rdf:Bag>
          <rdf:li>Fanworks</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Teen And Up Audiences</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>She-Ra and the Princesses of Power (2018)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Adora/Catra (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Adora (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Glimmer (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Bow (She-Ra)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Catra (She-Ra) (briefly)</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Frustrated artists</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Not-so subtle critiques of the music industry</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Gratuitous abuse of italics</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Adora curses about as much as Catra</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>She and Glimmer both have repressed anger issues</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>And some subtle shade thrown at Light Hope for good measure</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Also hope you're ready to wax lyrical about music</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>"Fellas is is gay to see your disappeared ex on TV and immediately lose your shit"</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>"After ten years and five pages of relentlessly pining for her"</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>allusions to Shadow Weaver's A+ Parenting</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>F/F</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>No Archive Warnings Apply</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Hurt/Comfort</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Serious Injuries</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Flashbacks to said serious injuries</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Some discussion of ableism</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Introducing 'No Chill Catradora'</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Along with Chaos Gremlin Glimmer</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Now with an actual rock concert!</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Reminiscing over shared experiences before taking a hard left into the Feelsâ„¢</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>-sax solo- REUNITED AND IT FEELS SO GOOD!</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Bag>
      </dc:subject>
      <dc:publisher>
        <rdf:Bag>
          <rdf:li>Archive of Our Own</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Bag>
      </dc:publisher>
      <dc:date>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>2019-10-27T21:00:00-03:00</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
      </dc:date>
      <dc:language>
        <rdf:Bag>
          <rdf:li>en</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Bag>
      </dc:language>
    </rdf:Description>
